{
  "_capture": {
    "backend_commit": "ea06b664b (orchid-calyx-backend PR #1704, branch claude/gate8-per-judge-auth, after repair round 1; unmerged). First captured at 5657dd07 and recaptured here after the blind-name contract changed.",
    "method": "FastAPI TestClient against app.show_app.create_show_app() on in-memory SQLite, using the synthetic show fixture from tests/test_judge_auth_blind_judging.py (synthetic exhibitors, judges and plants; no real show data)",
    "server_config": "CALYX_API_KEY and CALYX_JUDGE_TOKEN_SECRET set to the backend test suite's capture-only values; the judge_me_unconfigured_503 scenario unsets CALYX_JUDGE_TOKEN_SECRET",
    "tokens": "The ocj_ tokens below were minted by that throwaway in-memory database with a test-only secret. They authenticate nothing on any deployed backend.",
    "sequence": "Captured in one run, in order: the event is open (not blind) for judge_plants_open and judge_scan_open, then set blind; the first plant carries a legacy id-derived tag until owner_reissue_qr_tokens; judge C is assigned only Paphiopedilum; judge A's credential is revoked just before judge_me_revoked_401, then retried with JUDGE_AUTH_FAILURE_LIMIT_PER_CREDENTIAL=2 for judge_me_rate_limited_429; after the event is set blind the owner sets one plant's blind_display_name (owner_set_blind_display_name) and tries an exhibitor-derived one (owner_set_blind_display_name_warning_409). owner_issue_without_owner_key_401 is an owner route called with no owner key (what a browser owner session receives on these routes today); owner_issue_unconfigured_503 is issuance with CALYX_JUDGE_TOKEN_SECRET unset.",
    "note": "Every entry is a real backend response (status + body). Any other error shape used in tests is labelled synthetic in that test."
  },
